                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "835b7315-1f5b-35ce-8da9-379438eb6380",
                        "entry_id": "cd149612-6631-3a61-a440-500cabf56f78",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A spiritual part of the soul in Egyptian mythology, which survived after death."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4714676c-7903-4c5a-b970-8601881bbfd4",
                                "sense_id": "835b7315-1f5b-35ce-8da9-379438eb6380",
                                "text": "Then, I wondered how long I must wait before seeing my Double, but if I recalled, the Ka was not supposed to appear before the seventy days of embalming were done."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c44a8b69-dd03-4060-8e3a-93b8ad91dc85",
                                "sense_id": "835b7315-1f5b-35ce-8da9-379438eb6380",
                                "text": "Hence Dorian's portrait is like the ka or double of the deceased in Egyptian tombs, heaped with toys and furniture."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c34f0cdc-698c-45fb-9865-ea0fccfada8f",
                                "sense_id": "835b7315-1f5b-35ce-8da9-379438eb6380",
                                "text": "‘You could bind the ka of a man to his body for five thousand years,’ said Jaquel."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
